-- UKMLA Clinical Pharmacology, Therapeutics and Prescribing safety -- Batch 1
-- 50 questions covering adverse drug reactions, anticoagulation & antiplatelet therapy,
-- drug interactions, pharmacokinetics, poisoning & overdose, prescribing in renal & hepatic
-- impairment, and safe prescribing & medication error.

  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 62-year-old woman with hypertension is reviewed in general practice. She started ramipril 6 weeks ago after her blood pressure remained elevated on amlodipine alone. She now reports a persistent dry, tickling cough for the last 3 weeks, with no wheeze, fever, or breathlessness. She has no history of asthma or reflux. Examination: chest clear, HR 74 bpm, BP 132/78 mmHg. Chest X-ray is normal.',
  'What is the most appropriate next step in management?',
  array['ACE inhibitor','cough','adverse drug reaction']
),
